course: dictionary
lesson: 903
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bitterness is a noun, a word for a thing you can taste or feel. It comes from the adjective bitter, and the ending -ness turns it into a noun meaning the quality of being bitter. A dictionary can give several meanings, so you need context to pick the right one.
explain: «Taste buds sense five basic tastes: sweet, salty, sour, bitter and umami.» This sentence is about taste, so bitterness here means a sharp, unpleasant taste. Ask yourself: does the meaning fit the sentence? A sharp taste fits; a sad feeling would not.
explain: «His home had called him, sorrowfully, reproachfully, but with no bitterness or anger.» Here the clue is anger. Bitterness means angry, hurt feelings because you think you were treated unfairly. Plaintive, meaning sad-sounding, is another clue that the mood is hurt, not tasty.
explain: The third meaning is about weather. The phrase «the bitterness of the wind» means very sharp coldness. When a word has more than one meaning, swap each meaning into the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: Bitterness is a noun, so it names a taste, a feeling or a kind of cold.
fact: «Bitterness» can mean a sharp, unpleasant taste, like strong coffee or dark chocolate.
fact: Your taste buds sense five basic tastes: sweet, salty, sour, bitter and umami.
fact: Many poisons taste bitter, so bitterness can warn us to stay away from harmful things.
fact: «Bitterness» can also mean angry, hurt feelings after being treated unfairly, or very sharp coldness in the weather.
exercise: «Many poisons taste bitter, so bitterness can warn us.» In this sentence, what does bitterness mean? | Angry, hurt feelings | *A sharp, unpleasant taste | Very sharp coldness | A sweet, sugary treat
exercise: «...with no bitterness or anger; only with plaintive reminder that it was there.» What does bitterness mean here? | *Angry, hurt feelings after being treated unfairly | A sour, salty taste | Sweet, pleasant happiness | Very sharp coldness
exercise: Lily shivered in «the bitterness of the wind». What does bitterness mean here? | Angry, hurt feelings | A sweet smell | *Very sharp coldness | A bitter cup of coffee
test: Which of the five basic tastes is the savoury taste of cheese and tomatoes? | Salty | Sweet | *Umami | Sour
test: Sam felt a deep ___ after the team let him down. Which word fits best? | Umami | *Bitterness | Sweetness | Saltiness
exam: Bitterness is a noun formed from an adjective. Which is that adjective? | *bitter | bittern | bitterly | bitterness
